---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="The Economics of High-Volume Activewear Wholesale: Maximizing Your ROI"
  description="A financial guide for activewear retailers on how to optimize procurement costs and increase margins on $25,000+ orders."
>
  <article class="py-32 max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 font-['Century_Gothic',sans-serif]">
    <header class="mb-16">
      <span class="text-accent font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">Financial Strategy</span>
      <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-black uppercase tracking-tighter mt-4 mb-8 font-['Montserrat',sans-serif]">The Economics of <span class="text-accent italic">High-Volume Wholesale</span></h2>
      <div class="flex items-center space-x-4 text-gray-500 text-sm">
        <span>Published: June 19, 2026</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>12 Min Read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
      <p class="text-xl text-black font-bold mb-8">When your order volume exceeds 3,000 pieces, every $0.10 in unit cost equates to $300 in profit. At Fitclo, we help you find those "hidden" margins.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-black uppercase mt-12 mb-6 font-['Montserrat',sans-serif]">1. The "Scale Curve" Discount</h2>
      <p>The biggest jump in profitability happens between the 500-piece tier and the 2,000-piece tier. By moving into $20k+ order territory, you unlock factory-direct raw material pricing. We pass our fabric-mill volume discounts directly to you, often reducing unit costs by 15-20%.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-black uppercase mt-12 mb-6 font-['Montserrat',sans-serif]">2. Amortizing Branding Costs</h2>
      <p>Custom heat-transfer labels and specialized hang-tags have fixed setup costs. On a 100-piece order, these add significantly to the unit price. On a 5,000-piece order, these costs are negligible. For high-volume buyers, premium branding becomes practically "free."</p>

      <div class="bg-accent/10 p-12 rounded-[40px] my-12">
        <h4 class="text-2xl font-black text-black mb-6 uppercase">Typical Margin Analysis:</h4>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
          <div>
            <span class="block font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase text-xs mb-2">Small Batch (300 Pcs)</span>
            <span class="text-3xl font-black text-black">35-45% Margin</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase text-xs mb-2">High Volume (3000 Pcs)</span>
            <span class="text-3xl font-black text-black">65-75% Margin</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-black uppercase mt-12 mb-6 font-['Montserrat',sans-serif]">3. Logistics Optimization</h2>
      <p>A $30,000 order allows for <strong>Sea Freight (LCL or FCL)</strong>. Compared to Air Express, Sea Freight can reduce your landed cost by up to 70%. For a high-volume retailer, shipping savings alone can fund your next collection.</p>
    </div>

    <footer class="mt-20 pt-10 border-t border-gray-100">
      <div class="bg-black text-white p-12 rounded-[40px] text-center">
        <h3 class="text-3xl font-black uppercase tracking-tighter mb-6">Boost Your Bottom Line</h3>
        <p class="mb-8 text-white/70">Contact our sales team for a custom quote on orders over 3,000 pieces.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="inline-block bg-accent text-black px-10 py-4 rounded-full font-black uppercase tracking-widest hover:scale-105 transition-transform">Get a Scale Quote</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
